  "tagline": "Embeddable JSON document database in C, with a JQL query language and optional HTTP/WebSocket server.",
  "description": "EJDB2 is a small C library that gives applications an embedded JSON document store, roughly what SQLite is to SQL. Documents live in collections in a single file on the iowow key-value engine, are queried with JQL (an XPath-like filter and projection language) and can use secondary indexes. An optional built-in HTTP/WebSocket endpoint can expose a database to other processes. Bindings cover Node.js, Java, Android, Swift, Flutter and React Native. The maintainer ships frequent point releases (v2.95 in October 2026). It suits desktop, mobile and IoT apps that want JSON documents without running a server.",
